################################################################################
#                           PKCE AUTH FLOW                                     #
#  Recommended if you have a browser available on your machine.                #
################################################################################


================================================================================
PKCE — Search-only profile
================================================================================

Use this when you only have access to the data services interface (search
endpoint). Your admin provides the full rag_search_api_endpoint_url.
Only the search tool will be available.

{
    "auth_flow": "pkce",
    "rag_search_api_endpoint_url": "https://10.0.0.2/api/data-engine/workspaces/00001111-aaaa-2222-bbbb-3333cccc4444/data-collections/55556666-dddd-7777-eeee-8888ffff9999/search",
    "verify_ssl": false,
    "token_request_endpoint_url": "https://login.microsoftonline.com/<tenant>/oauth2/v2.0/authorize",
    "token_exchange_endpoint_url": "https://login.microsoftonline.com/<tenant>/oauth2/v2.0/token",
    "token_request_params": {
        "client_id": "00001111-aaaa-2222-bbbb-3333cccc4444",
        "redirect_uri": "http://localhost:8888",
        "scope": "api://your-app/.default",
        "use_pkce": true,
        "auth_timeout_seconds": 300
    }
}


================================================================================
PKCE — Full access (explicit) profile
================================================================================

Use this when you have access to both the cluster management interface and the
data services interface, and want to specify each base URL explicitly. All tools
for your persona will be available. The search tool requires you to pass
workspace_uuid and datacollection_uuid explicitly.

{
    "auth_flow": "pkce",
    "base_url": "https://10.0.0.1/api",
    "data_services_base_url": "https://10.0.0.2/api",
    "verify_ssl": false,
    "token_request_endpoint_url": "https://login.microsoftonline.com/<tenant>/oauth2/v2.0/authorize",
    "token_exchange_endpoint_url": "https://login.microsoftonline.com/<tenant>/oauth2/v2.0/token",
    "token_request_params": {
        "client_id": "00001111-aaaa-2222-bbbb-3333cccc4444",
        "redirect_uri": "http://localhost:8888",
        "scope": "api://your-app/.default",
        "use_pkce": true,
        "auth_timeout_seconds": 300
    }
}


================================================================================
PKCE — Full access (mixed) profile
================================================================================

Use this when you have access to both interfaces but want the search tool to
default to a pre-configured workspace and data collection (parsed from the
rag_search_api_endpoint_url). The data_services_base_url is derived
automatically from the search URL.

{
    "auth_flow": "pkce",
    "base_url": "https://10.0.0.1/api",
    "rag_search_api_endpoint_url": "https://10.0.0.2/api/data-engine/workspaces/00001111-aaaa-2222-bbbb-3333cccc4444/data-collections/55556666-dddd-7777-eeee-8888ffff9999/search",
    "verify_ssl": false,
    "token_request_endpoint_url": "https://login.microsoftonline.com/<tenant>/oauth2/v2.0/authorize",
    "token_exchange_endpoint_url": "https://login.microsoftonline.com/<tenant>/oauth2/v2.0/token",
    "token_request_params": {
        "client_id": "00001111-aaaa-2222-bbbb-3333cccc4444",
        "redirect_uri": "http://localhost:8888",
        "scope": "api://your-app/.default",
        "use_pkce": true,
        "auth_timeout_seconds": 300
    }
}


################################################################################
#                        DEVICE CODE AUTH FLOW                                 #
#  Use this if you do not have a browser on your machine. A short code will    #
#  be printed in the logs — copy it, open the provided verification URL on     #
#  any device, and enter the code to complete authentication.                  #
################################################################################


================================================================================
Device Code — Search-only profile
================================================================================

Use this when you only have access to the data services interface (search
endpoint). Your admin provides the full rag_search_api_endpoint_url.
Only the search tool will be available.

{
    "auth_flow": "device_code",
    "rag_search_api_endpoint_url": "https://10.0.0.2/api/data-engine/workspaces/00001111-aaaa-2222-bbbb-3333cccc4444/data-collections/55556666-dddd-7777-eeee-8888ffff9999/search",
    "verify_ssl": false,
    "device_code_endpoint_url": "https://login.microsoftonline.com/<tenant>/oauth2/v2.0/devicecode",
    "token_request_endpoint_url": "https://login.microsoftonline.com/<tenant>/oauth2/v2.0/token",
    "token_request_params": {
        "client_id": "00001111-aaaa-2222-bbbb-3333cccc4444",
        "scope": "api://your-app/.default"
    }
}


================================================================================
Device Code — Full access (explicit) profile
================================================================================

Use this when you have access to both the cluster management interface and the
data services interface, and want to specify each base URL explicitly. All tools
for your persona will be available. The search tool requires you to pass
workspace_uuid and datacollection_uuid explicitly.

{
    "auth_flow": "device_code",
    "base_url": "https://10.0.0.1/api",
    "data_services_base_url": "https://10.0.0.2/api",
    "verify_ssl": false,
    "device_code_endpoint_url": "https://login.microsoftonline.com/<tenant>/oauth2/v2.0/devicecode",
    "token_request_endpoint_url": "https://login.microsoftonline.com/<tenant>/oauth2/v2.0/token",
    "token_request_params": {
        "client_id": "00001111-aaaa-2222-bbbb-3333cccc4444",
        "scope": "api://your-app/.default"
    }
}


================================================================================
Device Code — Full access (mixed) profile
================================================================================

Use this when you have access to both interfaces but want the search tool to
default to a pre-configured workspace and data collection (parsed from the
rag_search_api_endpoint_url). The data_services_base_url is derived
automatically from the search URL.

{
    "auth_flow": "device_code",
    "base_url": "https://10.0.0.1/api",
    "rag_search_api_endpoint_url": "https://10.0.0.2/api/data-engine/workspaces/00001111-aaaa-2222-bbbb-3333cccc4444/data-collections/55556666-dddd-7777-eeee-8888ffff9999/search",
    "verify_ssl": false,
    "device_code_endpoint_url": "https://login.microsoftonline.com/<tenant>/oauth2/v2.0/devicecode",
    "token_request_endpoint_url": "https://login.microsoftonline.com/<tenant>/oauth2/v2.0/token",
    "token_request_params": {
        "client_id": "00001111-aaaa-2222-bbbb-3333cccc4444",
        "scope": "api://your-app/.default"
    }
}


################################################################################
#                          KEY REFERENCE                                       #
################################################################################

Endpoint keys (at least one required):
  base_url                     Cluster management interface, e.g. https://10.0.0.1/api
                               Required for all tools except search.
  data_services_base_url       Data services interface, e.g. https://10.0.0.2/api
                               Required for search. Auto-derived from
                               rag_search_api_endpoint_url if omitted.
  rag_search_api_endpoint_url  Full pre-built search URL including workspace and
                               data-collection UUIDs. When present,
                               default_workspace_uuid and default_datacollection_uuid
                               are parsed from the URL automatically.

Auth keys (always required):
  auth_flow                    "pkce" or "device_code"
  token_request_endpoint_url   OAuth2 authorization endpoint (PKCE) or token
                               endpoint (device code)
  token_request_params         Object with client_id and auth-flow-specific params

Auth keys (conditional):
  token_exchange_endpoint_url  Token endpoint for PKCE (required if different
                               from token_request_endpoint_url)
  device_code_endpoint_url     Device code endpoint (required when auth_flow
                               is "device_code")

Other:
  verify_ssl                   true or false — whether to verify TLS certificates
